dialogue cohesion_barbarian_cleric
title: Clean wraps
trigger: Cohesion barbarian cleric level=2
once
speaker commander $commander
speaker barbarian barbarian
speaker cleric cleric

node open commander
  By the wagon wheel the Cleric has a roll of clean bandage out and is holding it toward the Barbarian, who has both fists tucked under both arms like a child hiding sweets.
  -> wraps

node wraps cleric
  Your knuckles are split to the bone and you're wrapping them in that. Choir white, off a tithe wagon, that's been on a dozen cuts. Let me do it properly.
  -> red

node red barbarian
  The white's mine. I bleed on it on purpose. And you were the one I couldn't tell from the slime, that day the red came up on me. You stood there. Why'd you stand there?
  -> places

node places cleric
  Because I've stood closer to worse. I wore that white, Barbarian. Six years at the tables. I don't know if I was ever at Saltmoss. I never learned the places. Only the people.
  * The Cleric walked away from the tables. That's the side that counts. -> vouched
    do: AddCohesion barbarian cleric 10
    do: AddTrust barbarian -3
    do: SetFlag barbarian_cleric:tables_vouched
  * Neither of you put anyone in that chair. The Choir did. -> shared
    do: AddCohesion barbarian cleric 6
    do: SetFlag barbarian_cleric:tables_shared
  * That's between the two of you. I won't take a side on it. -> apart
    do: AddCohesion barbarian cleric -4
    do: AddTrust cleric 2
    do: SetFlag barbarian_cleric:tables_apart
  * When the red comes, I shout Saltmoss. Let the Cleric shout it too. -> word
    if: FlagSet barbarian:rage_word
    do: AddCohesion barbarian cleric 10
    do: SetFlag barbarian_cleric:tables_word

node vouched barbarian
  Easy for you to say, Commander. You weren't sat by the door all winter. But aye. Walked away. That's more than the collector at our well ever did.
  -> book

node shared barbarian
  The Choir. Aye. It's a big word to hate. Easier to hate one face. I'll try the big word for a while.
  -> book

node apart barbarian
  Fine. We'll sort it ourselves, then. We usually do.
  -> book

node word barbarian
  Saltmoss, from a healer's mouth. Huh. If you shout it, I'll know it's meant. Nobody shouts that word by accident.
  -> book

node book cleric
  I keep a book of names. If there's anyone from Saltmoss in it, I'd like you to know who. If there isn't, I'd like to write someone down. You choose who.
  * Look through it together, both of you, by the same lamp. -> together
    do: AddCohesion barbarian cleric 8
    do: AddTrust cleric -2
    do: SetFlag barbarian_cleric:book_together
  * Ash. Write Ash in it, as a living name and not a lost one. -> ash
    if: FlagSet barbarian:thread_him
    do: AddCohesion barbarian cleric 10
    do: AddTrust barbarian 3
    do: SetFlag barbarian_cleric:book_ash
  * Tell the Barbarian about Wren. -> wren
    if: FlagSet cleric:thread_girl
    do: AddCohesion barbarian cleric 8
    do: SetFlag barbarian_cleric:book_wren
  * Some books are better left shut tonight. -> shut
    do: AddCohesion barbarian cleric -2
    do: AddTrust barbarian 2
    do: SetFlag barbarian_cleric:book_shut

node together barbarian
  Same lamp. Go on, then. Read me the names slow. I'm not much for reading, but I'll know a Saltmoss name when I hear one.
  -> close

node ash barbarian
  Living. Aye. Write it big. A-S-H. Not in the back with the lost ones. Up front, where you'd put someone you were going to see again.
  -> close

node wren barbarian
  Twelve, and she asked if the colour went somewhere nice. Moors take it. Give me the bandage, Cleric. I'll wear it under the white, if that's how you want it.
  -> close

node shut barbarian
  Shut's fine. I've no head for names tonight. My hands, though. You can have my hands.
  -> close

node close commander
  The Barbarian holds out both fists. The Cleric wraps them in clean linen, then winds the white cloth back over the top, turn by turn, and ties it off with steady fingers.
